(A list passed to a value parameter is copied into it: freeing the list by
 its own name inside the function leaves the parameter whole
 (docs/BUGS_FOUND.md #143 (d)).)
a list called xs is ["a", "b"].
To 'look at' with a value called v.
    Free xs.
    Print "v: {v}".

'look at' of xs.
Print "xs: {xs}".
